WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.945
A rocket engine carries its own fuel and oxygen.

2
00:00:02.945 --> 00:00:05.185
That’s why it can work without air.

3
00:00:05.185 --> 00:00:06.725
These pumps push the liquids down

4
00:00:06.725 --> 00:00:08.325
into the chamber below.

5
00:00:08.325 --> 00:00:10.105
There, they mix and burn,

6
00:00:10.105 --> 00:00:12.370
making very hot gas under high pressure.

7
00:00:12.765 --> 00:00:14.965
The gas flows through this narrow throat.

8
00:00:14.965 --> 00:00:16.465
In the wider nozzle beyond it,

9
00:00:16.465 --> 00:00:18.745
the gas expands and speeds up.

10
00:00:18.745 --> 00:00:20.285
As the engine throws gas down,

11
00:00:20.285 --> 00:00:22.285
the gas pushes the rocket up.

12
00:00:22.285 --> 00:00:24.910
The engine turns stored chemical energy into motion.
